+## Novelty / duplicate-avoidance audit (P-002, 2026-11-26, run 45760979765 slot 03)
+
+- **Question:** Does the durable history adequately prevent repeating equivalent experiments when a frontier cell is already resolved?
+- **Conclusion: RETAIN — the minimal novelty guard is sufficient.** The frontier table above lists each resolved signal-class cell exactly once with a terminal status (FALSIFIED / TESTED / COST_ROBUST / REJECTED); the campaign selector (`.github/scripts/campaign_controller.py::select_task` + `load_queue`) enforces exact `task_id` deduplication and ordinal priority over OPEN tasks; the prompt firewall and Learning rule 2 forbid equivalent re-tests. Across campaign agents 01–03 (P-001, R-001, P-002) no equivalent experiment was executed twice.
+- **One concrete near-duplicate found (pre-campaign manual phase, no artifact):** `research/checks/momentum_sweep.py` (lookbacks 3/5/10/20) is redundant with the ADMITTED `research/checks/momentum_lookback_sweep.py` (3/5/10; artifact `momentum_lookback_sweep_results.json`) plus `research/checks/momentum_longer_horizon.py` (20/60). It has no artifact and is referenced by no durable record. **Do not re-run it as a new experiment — treat it as superseded.**
+- **Residual (not a current bottleneck):** the controller has no *semantic* (near-duplicate) novelty check — only exact `task_id` — so prevention relies on the frontier table plus agent discipline. That has held so far; a code-level guard is out of scope and not warranted without an observed executed duplicate.
